  temptable_boundary  bulk_cool
! HEADER: 
!  This is the initial fuel temperature table 
!  The goal of this table is to provide fuel temperatures as a function of power 
!  an burnup as follows: 
!    Tfuel = Tmod + a * P  + b * P^2  where a and b are functions of burnup and P is the linear heat flux 
! 
!  The structure of this file is very basic.  A header will give the number of burnup points and the linear 
!  heat rate used to generate the file.  (this is so the data can be fit using normalized powers, if actual 
!  linear heat rates are used in the computation of a and b, enter 1.0 for the LHR. 
!  The header is followed by a list of a and b for each burnup point (in GWD/MT) 
! 
!                    LHR (W/cm) 
  temptable_qprime     0.974
!  list of temperature coefficients 
!  Bu (GWD/MT)    a (K)        b (K)
  temptable_polynomial
      0.00     2.64920235   -0.00192506
     10.00     1.72317832    0.00033787
